# 🚀 Performance Optimization Guidelines

## Executive Summary

This document provides comprehensive performance standards and optimization techniques for both `atlas-web` (React) and `atlas-native` (React Native) component libraries. Following these guidelines will ensure:

- ⚡ **Fast Initial Load**: Optimized bundle size and resource loading
- 🔄 **Efficient Rendering**: Minimized re-renders and DOM/native operations
- 📱 **Smooth Interactions**: 60fps animations and responsive user interactions
- 🧠 **Resource Efficiency**: Optimized memory usage and reduced battery impact

---

## 💯 Performance Metrics & Targets

| Metric | atlas-web Target | atlas-native Target | Measurement Tool |
|--------|------------------|---------------------|------------------|
| **Initial Render** | < 150ms | < 250ms | React DevTools, Performance marks |
| **Re-render Time** | < 10ms | < 16ms (60fps) | React DevTools, Profiler API |
| **Bundle Size** | < 100KB (gzipped) | < 2MB (per screen) | Webpack Bundle Analyzer, Metro |
| **Memory Usage** | < 60MB (main bundle) | < 150MB (iOS/Android) | Chrome DevTools, Xcode Instruments |
| **Interaction Response** | < 100ms | < 100ms | Performance API, React Native Profiler |
| **Time-to-Interactive** | < 3s (3G) | < 2s (app startup) | Lighthouse, React Native Performance |

