## 🚦 Performance Testing in CI/CD

### Web Performance Testing

```yaml
# Example GitHub Action for web performance testing
name: Web Performance Testing

on:
  pull_request:
    paths:
      - 'packages/atlas-web/**'

jobs:
  lighthouse:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - name: Run Lighthouse CI
        uses: treosh/lighthouse-ci-action@v9
        with:
          urls: |
            https://staging.example.com/
          budgetPath: ./lighthouse-budget.json
          uploadArtifacts: true
          
  bundle-analysis:
    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
    steps:
      - uses: actions/checkout@v3
      - name: Setup Node.js
        uses: actions/setup-node@v3
      - name: Install dependencies
        run: npm ci
      - name: Build with bundle analysis
        run: npm run build:analyze
      - name: Check bundle size
        uses: jackfranklin/check-bundle-size-action@main
        with:
          github-token: ${{ secrets.GITHUB_TOKEN }}
          bundleSize: ./bundle-stats.json
          thresholds: |
            main.js=100KB
            vendors.js=250KB
```

### Native Performance Testing

```yaml
# Example GitHub Action for native performance testing
name: Native Performance Testing

on:
